  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong, central baseline to anchor the search. config_009 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) combines the most capable and standard choices across all design axes: it uses all modalities, the richer multiprofile setting, a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200), the stronger image backbone (ViT-L), a simple and robust aggregation (avgpool), and a flexible weighted fusion. This configuration has the highest prior probability of performing well and serves as a natural hub: every other multimodal configuration differs from it by only one or two factors, making it ideal for interpreting subsequent single-factor comparisons. Testing it first maximizes information gain per experiment under the 10-run budget."
}

